# Diabetes Prediction System

##  Overview
This is a Machine Learning-based web application that predicts whether a person is diabetic or not based on health parameters like glucose, BMI, insulin, blood pressure, age, and more. The project uses multiple ML models to compare performance and improve accuracy for early diabetes detection.



##  Features
- Predicts diabetes using medical input features  
- Web-based UI using Flask  
- Real-time prediction system  
- Model comparison for better accuracy  
- Simple and user-friendly interface  



##  Machine Learning Models Used
- Logistic Regression  
- Decision Tree  
- K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)  



##  Dataset
- Source: Kaggle  
- Features used:
  - Glucose
  - Blood Pressure
  - BMI
  - Insulin
  - Age
  - Skin Thickness  



##  Tech Stack
- Python  
- Flask  
- Scikit-learn  
- Pandas & NumPy  
- HTML, CSS  



##  Project Structure
Diabetes-Detection-Website/
│
├── app.py
├── diabetes_model.pkl
├── requirements.txt
├── README.md
│
├── static/
│   └── style.css
│
├── templates/
│   └── index.html



## Setup Instructions

### 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/your-username/Diabetes-Detection-Website.git

### 2. Move into project folder
cd Diabetes-Detection-Website

### 3. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

### 4. Run the application
python app.py



## How It Works
1. User enters medical details  
2. Data is processed by ML model  
3. Model predicts diabetes risk  
4. Result is shown on web page  



